    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ one pass
    ('h1', 'How one pass runs'),
    ('steps', [
        '**Start.** The Build VMs tab (the first time) or Turn On in the Cloud VMs pane (afterwards) starts the VM. The run step starts the job detached, so closing the PC does not stop it.',
        '**Credentials.** The job asks Google for a token as the service account, reads the three secrets, and asks Dropbox for an access token. It renews the access token by itself every 4 hours.',
        '**Inventory.** It lists the roots from the saved cursor: every file that is new, changed or deleted since the last run. The first run lists everything. A row is the file\u2019s id, path, size, dates and content hash.',
        '**Queue.** The files to analyse are the images whose content hash the catalog does not hold yet. A file that is an exact copy of another is analysed once.',
        '**Fetch and analyse,** several photos at a time. For each photo: download the original into memory; read the capture date, the GPS position, the camera and the orientation from its EXIF; make a working copy 1,024 pixels wide; compute the CLIP class scores and the 512-number embedding; find the faces and their 128-number embeddings; compute the album engine\u2019s quality metrics, difference hash and colour signature; read the text when CLIP says the image is text; save a 400-pixel thumbnail; write the row; discard the original.',
        '**Failures.** A photo that cannot be read is recorded with the reason and tried again on the next run. When Dropbox answers that requests come too fast, the job waits the number of seconds Dropbox states.',
        '**Group.** After the last photo: events, moments, groups of faces, names from the tagged examples, and event names from the date and the place. A few minutes for the whole bank.',
        '**Publish.** The catalog and a run report (counts, failures by reason, photos a second) are copied to the bucket.',
        '**Stop.** The job powers the VM off. What still costs is its disk, until the VM is deleted; the catalog is safe in the bucket either way.',
        '**On the PC.** Sync catalog in the Library tab copies the bucket to this PC.']),
    ('p', 'Videos are listed with their size and date and are not analysed in the first version. A pass can be stopped at any point: every photo is committed as it finishes, and the next run continues from there. That is also what makes a Spot VM safe to use.'),

